    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/post-doc-research-fellow-a-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Post doc Research Fellow A",
      "description": "Post doc Research Fellow A - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Post doc Research Fellow A Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Level A Fixed term - Full-time Level A Add to favourites View favourites Based in College of Engineering, Information & Technology at the City East Campus Full-time, fixed term contract for up to 24 months Salary Range: Level A $103,962 - $111,384 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters This position is for the design of materials for advanced energy storage and conversion devices. Work includes designing and synthesizing high-performance electrode materials and electrolyte systems, conducting various characterizations, designing testing compartments, and testing for battery performance. Develop next-generation materials for advanced energy storage and conversion technologies, with a focus on high-performance electrodes, electrolytes and battery systems. This research will contribute to innovative and sustainable energy solutions with the potential to support the transition towards a cleaner energy future. The team The successful candidate will work under the supervision of Professor Shizhang Qiao within a collaborative research team focused on advanced materials for energy storage and conversion. The team brings together expertise in materials chemistry, electrochemistry and battery technologies to address key challenges in sustainable energy and support the transition towards a low-carbon future. Visit the AU website to learn more about School of Chemical Engineering . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. The successful applicant will join a collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment within the School of Chemical Engineering, working alongside scientists and engineers with diverse expertise in materials science, electrochemistry and energy technologies. The role offers opportunities to undertake fundamental research using cutting-edge materials synthesis and advanced characterisation techniques, while collaborating closely with leading researchers in Australia and internationally. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: A recent PhD degree in Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, Material Science or related field. Expertise in the synthesis of functional materials and their application in aqueous batteries, or flow cells. Strong background in energy storage and conversion devices such as pouch cells, cylindrical cells, redox flow cells, etc. Knowledge and experience in modern materials characterization methodologies, such as Microscopy, and in-situ spectroscopy. Excellent track record in scientific journal publications. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm, Thursday 24 September 2026 Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493451) : Evelyn Ruth Talent Acquisition Advisor +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
