    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/data-engineer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Data Engineer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Data Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Engineering HEO7 Fixed term - Full-time HEO7 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Business Intelligence team at the City West campus Full-time 24 month fixed term contract Salary Range: $103,719 - $116,002 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Ensure the integrity, accessibility, and quality of data assets At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Enable data-driven decision-making by designing, developing, and maintaining robust data pipelines, models, and solutions that support the Adelaide University’s strategic and operational objectives. The role ensures the integrity, accessibility, and quality of data assets to empower business intelligence and analytics across the institution. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Business Intelligence team within the Performance, Data and Insights Function and is aligned to the Corporate Portfolio within the University. The Data Engineer will work most closely with the Chief Data and Analytics Officer, Director, Business Intelligence, and the IT and Finance teams. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Corporate Portfolio . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience in data manipulation, preparation, and integration Experience in designing, developing, and supporting data pipelines, models, and processes Proficiency in data management and business intelligence concepts and practices Experience with data manipulation tools and/or programming languages such as Power Query, Alteryx, SQL, and R Experience in stakeholder engagement, expectations, and relationship management Advanced Microsoft Office skills Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 13 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493457): Alexandra Koszegi Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/teaching-casuals-au-online-2026-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2026",
      "description": "Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2026 - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2026 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Casual Campaign Casual Casual rates apply Add to favourites View favourites At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand, and do you possess specialist knowledge and skills to teach in the fields of: Business & Law Creative Arts, Design and Humanities Education, Behavioural and Social Sciences Engineering and Information Technology Health and/or Science? With degrees spanning a wide range of programs, Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. About Adelaide University Online Adelaide University Online (AUO) offers a range of 100% online degrees and aspires to be the best online education provider in Australia. Our programs are delivered across two distinct models: 10-week periods delivered over 4 terms per year 6-week periods delivered over 6 terms per year Targeted at busy adults who need to juggle work, life and family commitments, AUO is making it possible for more people to integrate study into their busy lives and pursue their career goals. Each degree has been specifically designed for online learning and is delivered in an engaging and flexible way. Students can access academics and study support out of hours and on weekends, so they can get help when they need it. Application Process: Please view the available courses through the application form, to determine what area of work offerings are being made available for individual. Ensure you meet the essential criteria – essential skills and experience listed below. Note: This is a fully remote, flexible role with work conducted primarily outside standard Monday to Friday, 9am-5pm office hours. Core Responsibilities Undertake online teaching as part of the AUO teaching team Apply disciplinary expertise to consult, facilitate discussions, mark assessment items, and provide feedback to students Implement approaches that maximise the student experience and learning outcomes Provide academic support, mentoring and advice to students Act as the first point of response/contact in managing student issues or complaints Essential Skills and Experience Minimum Bachelor’s degree and relevant professional/industry work experience (10-week courses) Minimum Masters or PhD (6-week courses) Ability to undertake a range of teaching duties in an online environment Ability to actively engage and educate a diverse student group Excellent written and interpersonal skills Ability to use the necessary digital techniques and tools required for effective online teaching Available to work outside of normal working hours, including weekends Please contact Academic and Program Services at auoacademic.programservices@adelaide.edu.au if you have any questions about this process. Please note, this email is for enquiries only. Applications will only be accepted through the online portal. Please note - By registering on the Casual/Sessional Staff Register, it does not guarantee that employment will be offered. If you already hold a casual contract with Adelaide University, please apply and complete the application form to be considered for future opportunities. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia and for the term of appointment. To be eligible, you will need to reside within Australia. Submit your application by 11:30pm Friday 18 September 2026 Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. #S-DNI #LI-DN Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
